{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (44.4%) to bacteria Plantaricin JLA-9. Chemical modification: This is a unique peptide that forms a new class UCSS1c. Darobactin has an unusual structure with two fused rings that form post-translationally. There is an unusual ether bond that links C6 of aromatic W1 and beta-carbon of W3. A second carbon-carbon bond connects C7 of aromatic W3 and beta-carbon of basic K5. Activity: Active against P. aeruginosa PAO1, P. aeruginosa pmrB 523C>T, S. sonnei ATCC 25931, K. pneumoniae ATCC 700603, K. pneumoniae ESBL JMI 1052654, E. coli ATCC 25922, E. coli AR350 (mcr-1), E. coli ESBL JMI 1043856, E. coli ATCC BAA-2340 (KPC), E. coli MG1655 +10% serum (all previous, MIC 2 ug/ml), K. pneumoniae ATCC 700603 (SHV-18), K. pneumoniae ATCC BAA-1705 (KPC), E. coli MG1655, S. Typhimurium LT2 ATCC 19585 (MIC 4 ug/ml), M. catarrhalis ATCC 25238, A. baumannii ATCC 17978 (MIC 8 ug/ml), P. aeruginosa JMI 1045324 (MIC 16 uM), E. cloacae ATCC 13047 (MIC 32 ug/ml), and P. mirabilis KLE 2600 (MIC 64 ug/ml). Not active agains the Gram+ bacteria tested. Resistance mechanism: Mutants that are resistant to darobactin map to BamA, an essential chaperone and translocator that folds outer membrane proteins. Animal model:mouse: thigh: a single injection of 50 mg/kg or 3 injections (every 6 h) significantly reduced bacteria at 26 h. The peptide also protects animals from death. In vivo PK:mouse: 50 mg/kg:IP: peak level 94 ug/ml and Peptide half life in blood is 1 h. In vitro toxicity: Interestingly, this peptide is not toxic to symbiotic gut bacteria, but ampicillin did. It is a potential lead. Updated 5/2024", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "31747680", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Nature. 2019;576(7787):459–464. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03168", "source_id": "AP03168", "source_numeric_id": "03168", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03168", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "A New Antibiotic Selectively Kills Gram-negative Pathogens", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
